 "_how_to_fill": "Each category has three lists: en (English as Kenyans write it), sw (Swahili) and sheng (Nairobi street Swahili-English mix). Add words people really type in WhatsApp and Telegram, including common misspellings and shortened forms. Rules: lowercase; one word or short phrase per entry (2 to 40 characters, letters, digits, spaces, apostrophe, hyphen, dot only); no regular expressions; end an entry with * to accept any ending (nyoa* matches nyoa, nyoaji, nyoaje) or + to accept a repeated last letter (hi+ matches hii, hiii). Do not remove existing entries. Do not add everyday function words (na, ya, ni, the, and, is): they would make every message look like salon talk. Return the same JSON with the lists filled.",
